/* Elsewhere Infinite Door v16: independently authored, local-only encounter library. */
(()=>{'use strict';const CONTENT={"forms":{"letter":[{"id":"letter-01","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"To whoever still remembers the old lighthouse: the lamp has been shining over a city with no sea. What do you write back?","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"},{"id":"letter-02","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"An unsigned letter apologizes for something nobody has done yet. Do you answer, investigate, or leave it sealed?","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"},{"id":"letter-03","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"A note from your future self contains only the words: 'Ask about the second door.' What do you ask?","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"},{"id":"letter-04","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"The Department of Lost Tuesdays requests an explanation for an hour that seems to be missing from everybody's week. Compose your reply.","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"},{"id":"letter-05","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"Someone returns a book you never lent them, with a letter thanking you for a conversation you never had. What happened?","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"},{"id":"letter-06","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"A letter addressed to the person you could have become is delivered to you by mistake. Do you open it?","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"},{"id":"letter-07","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"The envelope contains a map of places where strangers made each other's days better. Add one stop.","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"},{"id":"letter-08","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"Someone writes: 'I have spent years confusing being understood with being agreed with.' What would you tell them?","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"},{"id":"letter-09","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"A former antagonist writes to the hero ten years after the story ended. What are they finally ready to admit?","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"},{"id":"letter-10","type":"letter","category":"unearth","text":"An invitation arrives for the unveiling of a statue honoring a tiny kindness nobody remembers performing. Who attends?","tags":["care","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What detail in the handwriting changes the interpretation?","doorLabel":"Turn over the envelope"}],"field":[{"id":"field-01","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"You are cataloguing an ordinary room for a future civilization. Which five objects explain its inhabitants best?","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"},{"id":"field-02","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"Observe a harmless habit in your day as though you were a patient field researcher. What does it accomplish?","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"},{"id":"field-03","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"An astronomer reports a star that appears only when nobody expects it. What instrument or assumption gets checked first?","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"},{"id":"field-04","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"Document a neighborhood custom whose origin everyone has forgotten. What competing explanations survive?","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"},{"id":"field-05","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"An archive contains hundreds of descriptions of the same sunrise, none identical. Choose the detail worth preserving.","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"},{"id":"field-06","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"Describe a place using only sounds. What does the listener infer incorrectly?","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"},{"id":"field-07","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"Record the lifespan of a repaired object: what can its scratches, tape, or replaced parts tell you?","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"},{"id":"field-08","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"Survey a familiar route as though it were undiscovered terrain. Where would an explorer stop?","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"},{"id":"field-09","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"Make a field note about a small decision you made automatically. What was the hidden rule?","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"},{"id":"field-10","type":"field","category":"notice","text":"Examine an everyday ritual without deciding whether it is good or bad. What need does it appear to serve?","tags":["curiosity","reflection"],"intensity":"light","door":"What observation might a different researcher challenge?","doorLabel":"Examine the margin note"}],"dialogue":[{"id":"dialogue-01","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"A cartographer and a poet disagree about what makes a place real. Write their last three lines.","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"},{"id":"dialogue-02","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"A curious child interviews a very old bridge. What does the bridge refuse to answer?","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"},{"id":"dialogue-03","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"Two people want the same quiet room for very different reasons. How do they negotiate?","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"},{"id":"dialogue-04","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"A historian and a time traveler argue about an event neither witnessed accurately. Who asks the better question?","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"},{"id":"dialogue-05","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"A confident detective and a skeptical librarian examine a clue that looks too obvious. What do they notice differently?","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"},{"id":"dialogue-06","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"An inventor explains a machine to the one person who will never need it. What does that person ask?","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"},{"id":"dialogue-07","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"One character says 'I thought you knew.' The other replies 'I thought you asked.' What happens next?","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"},{"id":"dialogue-08","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"Two former rivals meet in the grocery aisle and agree not to talk about their rivalry. What do they talk about instead?","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"},{"id":"dialogue-09","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"A mountain interviews a hiker. For once, the mountain gets to ask the questions.","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"},{"id":"dialogue-10","type":"dialogue","category":"imagine","text":"A tired superhero and a night-shift cleaner share a break. Which one understands the city better?","tags":["care","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would the quietest participant say now?","doorLabel":"Hear an unheard reply"}],"dilemma":[{"id":"dilemma-01","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"You can preserve one memory perfectly or allow all of them to change naturally. What would make the choice difficult?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"},{"id":"dilemma-02","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"A city can fix its oldest landmark only by changing it beyond recognition. Who should have a say?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"},{"id":"dilemma-03","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"You discover a rule that keeps people safe but excludes the very people it was meant to protect. What changes first?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"},{"id":"dilemma-04","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"A friend asks for reassurance about something you genuinely cannot know. How can you be kind without inventing certainty?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"},{"id":"dilemma-05","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"An inventor offers a tool that makes decisions easier but makes mistakes harder to learn from. Do you accept it?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"},{"id":"dilemma-06","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"A rescue plan helps most people but requires one uninvolved person to make a sacrifice. Who has authority to decide?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"},{"id":"dilemma-07","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"A museum has one empty exhibit space and ten communities who want it. How do they choose fairly?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"},{"id":"dilemma-08","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"You can correct a public misunderstanding but must reveal someone's harmless private detail to do it. What stays unsaid?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"},{"id":"dilemma-09","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"An old promise conflicts with a new and legitimate boundary. What matters when interpreting it?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"},{"id":"dilemma-10","type":"dilemma","category":"reframe","text":"A fictional kingdom gives every visitor one veto on local customs. What unforeseen fairness problem follows?","tags":["conviction","reflection"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Whose consent or boundary has not been considered?","doorLabel":"Reveal the omitted condition"}],"museum":[{"id":"museum-01","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"Exhibit 01: The Last Unsent Message. Write the label without pretending to know its author.","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"},{"id":"museum-02","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"The Museum of Everyday Courage displays a pair of worn shoes. Describe the act they witnessed.","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"},{"id":"museum-03","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"An exhibition contains an empty frame titled 'The Place Someone Finally Said No.' What should the guide explain?","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"},{"id":"museum-04","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"The museum acquires a repaired teacup with a story nobody can corroborate. How should the label express uncertainty?","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"},{"id":"museum-05","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"A gallery of impossible maps has one of a city that no longer exists. Which feature makes it recognizable?","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"},{"id":"museum-06","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"Curate three ordinary objects representing a friendship without naming either friend.","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"},{"id":"museum-07","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"A display of lost inventions includes a machine designed to make waiting easier. What did it accidentally change?","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"},{"id":"museum-08","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"Someone donates the sound of their childhood kitchen. What should the audio guide ask listeners to notice?","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"},{"id":"museum-09","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"The exhibit's object is a scratched key whose lock is gone. Invent three incompatible but equally plausible stories.","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"},{"id":"museum-10","type":"museum","category":"sacred","text":"A museum director asks you to name the one thing a collection must never pretend to know. Answer on its front wall.","tags":["reflection","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What can the exhibit not honestly claim?","doorLabel":"Open the curator's drawer"}],"ritual":[{"id":"ritual-01","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"Create a thirty-second ceremony for finishing a task nobody saw you do.","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"},{"id":"ritual-02","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"Invent an annual holiday celebrating a small kind of repair rather than an achievement.","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"},{"id":"ritual-03","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"Give an ordinary object a ceremonial title for the day. What does it now stand for?","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"},{"id":"ritual-04","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"Imagine a community that marks reconciliations by changing a public garden. What grows there?","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"},{"id":"ritual-05","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"Design a ritual for letting an unanswered question remain unanswered overnight.","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"},{"id":"ritual-06","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"Write a toast for the moment somebody asks a better question rather than winning an argument.","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"},{"id":"ritual-07","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"Choose three words for a private ritual honoring something you no longer want to carry.","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"},{"id":"ritual-08","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"A fictional culture thanks its bridges each year. What happened to inspire the custom?","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"},{"id":"ritual-09","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"Invent a tiny ceremony welcoming a newcomer without requiring them to disclose personal details.","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"},{"id":"ritual-10","type":"ritual","category":"sacred","text":"Imagine a celebration that only lasts until the next rain. What makes its impermanence valuable?","tags":["care","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"How did the ritual change as its meaning changed?","doorLabel":"Read the older custom"}],"casefile":[{"id":"casefile-01","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 14: Every public clock stopped at a different time. Investigate the most ordinary explanation first.","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"},{"id":"casefile-02","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 02: A stranger appears in two photographs separated by a century. List what the evidence can and cannot prove.","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"},{"id":"casefile-03","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 31: Neighbors disagree over the same sound. Which questions would reveal what they actually heard?","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"},{"id":"casefile-04","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 19: A library book has been checked out continuously since the building opened. Where does the record become unreliable?","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"},{"id":"casefile-05","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 40: A tiny town reports no arguments in twenty years. What would you investigate before celebrating?","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"},{"id":"casefile-06","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 07: Somebody has been planting flowers in abandoned places. Design a non-intrusive investigation.","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"},{"id":"casefile-07","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 24: The mayor claims an impossible invention works. Write three fair ways to test it.","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"},{"id":"casefile-08","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 11: A vanished street appears in official maps but nobody can recall walking there. Which source matters?","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"},{"id":"casefile-09","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 35: Two witnesses describe opposite intentions behind the same gesture. Separate their observations from interpretation.","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"},{"id":"casefile-10","type":"casefile","category":"learn","text":"Case 26: An unsigned note warns that the next clue is the obvious one. How would you avoid being led?","tags":["curiosity","focus"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which fact is known, and which is only an inference?","doorLabel":"Unseal the second report"}],"counterfactual":[{"id":"counterfactual-01","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if embarrassment had a short expiration date? Which ordinary choices would people make differently?","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"},{"id":"counterfactual-02","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if public spaces were designed first for people who needed rest? How would a city change?","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"},{"id":"counterfactual-03","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if every apology had to name a specific repair but nobody was obliged to forgive? Explore the result.","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"},{"id":"counterfactual-04","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if stories could be borrowed like books but memories couldn't? What would authors protect?","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"},{"id":"counterfactual-05","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if people were allowed to revise an opinion publicly without being punished for changing their mind?","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"},{"id":"counterfactual-06","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if every important decision included an explicit option to wait? What systems might slow down?","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"},{"id":"counterfactual-07","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if all historical monuments came with a counterpoint written by someone who disagreed?","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"},{"id":"counterfactual-08","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if a dream could become public property? Who would resist that rule?","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"},{"id":"counterfactual-09","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if every job came with one guaranteed hour of curiosity? Which discovery would matter?","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"},{"id":"counterfactual-10","type":"counterfactual","category":"reframe","text":"What if a town measured prosperity by the number of unanswered good questions?","tags":["imagination","conviction"],"intensity":"light","door":"Who benefits, and who bears an unchosen cost?","doorLabel":"Read the side-effect memo"}],"microfiction":[{"id":"microfiction-01","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"At midnight, the vending machine offered exactly one item: a second chance to ask a question. What happened?","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"},{"id":"microfiction-02","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"The astronomer noticed the stars spelling out a simple apology, but to whom?","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"},{"id":"microfiction-03","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"The tiny dragon worked at the complaint counter and was remarkably good at listening. What complaint changed its life?","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"},{"id":"microfiction-04","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"A gardener found an unlabelled plant that only grew where people changed their minds. What did it reveal?","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"},{"id":"microfiction-05","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"The last person in the town who could remember tomorrow opened a bakery. What was on the menu?","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"},{"id":"microfiction-06","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"Every year the city elected an official fool. This time, the fool refused the title. What changed?","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"},{"id":"microfiction-07","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"The hero returned to the village after defeating the monster. Nobody wanted the monster gone. Why?","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"},{"id":"microfiction-08","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"A paper boat floated uphill, carrying the name of someone who had never been born. Who followed it?","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"},{"id":"microfiction-09","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"A woman collected sounds from rooms after everyone left. One evening a sound followed her home.","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"},{"id":"microfiction-10","type":"microfiction","category":"imagine","text":"The lighthouse keeper finally learned what the light was meant to warn people about: silence.","tags":["imagination","play"],"intensity":"light","door":"Which ordinary detail makes the impossible believable?","doorLabel":"Read the next line"}],"play":[{"id":"play-01","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Give the most boring object in the room an outrageous job title and three impossible responsibilities.","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"},{"id":"play-02","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Invent a terrible theme park ride based on a household chore. Include the warning sign.","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"},{"id":"play-03","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Describe a cooking competition judged entirely by very judgmental furniture.","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"},{"id":"play-04","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Hold a fictional press conference about a missing sock. What question ends the briefing?","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"},{"id":"play-05","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Name a ludicrous award for a real, tiny success of today. Write its acceptance speech.","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"},{"id":"play-06","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Invent the world's least intimidating supervillain and their surprisingly persuasive manifesto.","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"},{"id":"play-07","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Pitch a television series in which the weather has terrible interpersonal boundaries.","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"},{"id":"play-08","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Write the instruction manual for a household appliance that believes it is a philosopher.","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"},{"id":"play-09","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Create a fictional public holiday for a very specific inconvenience. What is the traditional food?","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"},{"id":"play-10","type":"play","category":"wander","text":"Describe an alien documentary attempting to explain why humans own so many kinds of spoons.","tags":["play","creativity"],"intensity":"light","door":"What makes the situation even more ridiculous without harming anyone?","doorLabel":"Open the absurd appendix"}],"reflection":[{"id":"reflection-01","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"You are allowed to rewrite one expectation without rewriting any facts. Which expectation changes?","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"},{"id":"reflection-02","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"Describe something you can appreciate without wanting it to continue.","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"},{"id":"reflection-03","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"Recall a moment where being precise was kinder than being reassuring. What made that possible?","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"},{"id":"reflection-04","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"Write a fair version of an argument that acknowledges something each person could be missing.","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"},{"id":"reflection-05","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"Which part of your day felt more like your own choice than your obligation?","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"},{"id":"reflection-06","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"Name a small thing you know about yourself that does not need to become a rule.","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"},{"id":"reflection-07","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"What does a genuine change of mind feel like before you have the words for it?","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"},{"id":"reflection-08","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"Consider a problem you keep solving for other people. What would happen if you asked instead?","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"},{"id":"reflection-09","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"Write about a quiet victory that would not look impressive in a photograph.","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"},{"id":"reflection-10","type":"reflection","category":"shadow","text":"What do you wish a future version of you would remember about this week without judging it?","tags":["reflection","independence"],"intensity":"deep","door":"Which part would be easier to approach without judgment?","doorLabel":"Find the gentler question"}],"map":[{"id":"map-01","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"Draw a map of a city where every street is named after a kind of question. Where would you go?","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"},{"id":"map-02","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"A lost map contains only paths that were never taken. Choose one and invent what lies at its end.","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"},{"id":"map-03","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"Make a three-stop walking tour of an imaginary neighborhood that celebrates unlikely friendships.","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"},{"id":"map-04","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"Invent a transit diagram connecting a memory, a possibility, and an unfinished thought.","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"},{"id":"map-05","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"Sketch the borders of a country that exists only during thunderstorms. Who belongs there?","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"},{"id":"map-06","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"Design a star chart for people who navigate by stories rather than constellations.","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"},{"id":"map-07","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"Map the route from a harmless misunderstanding to a surprising discovery.","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"},{"id":"map-08","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"Create a subway line whose stations are feelings nobody can explain in one word.","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"},{"id":"map-09","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"Describe an atlas showing not territories but things people have agreed to share.","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"},{"id":"map-10","type":"map","category":"imagine","text":"Invent an island whose coastline changes according to the questions visitors ask.","tags":["curiosity","imagination"],"intensity":"light","door":"What would a person who lives here know that the map cannot show?","doorLabel":"Examine the unmarked route"}]},"trails":[{"id":"city","title":"The City That Forgot Its Name","kind":"imagine","steps":["At the city gate, a librarian asks whether you came to remember something or discover something. Answer, and describe the gate.","In the archive you find three names scratched out of the founding map. What might each have protected?","At the fountain, a stranger offers a memory of the city in exchange for an honest question. What question do you choose?","Before leaving you may name the city, refuse to name it, or ask its inhabitants to decide. What happens?"]},{"id":"museum","title":"The Museum of Almosts","kind":"unearth","steps":["Step into an exhibition of things that almost happened. Choose the first safe, ordinary exhibit.","A curator shows a second version of the same event. What detail changes without changing the facts?","One display contains a doorway labelled 'What I No Longer Need to Prove.' What would you place there?","The museum offers you a blank label to take home. What does it say?"]},{"id":"correspondence","title":"Letters from Elsewhere","kind":"wander","steps":["A letter arrives from a stranger asking for directions to a place that doesn't exist. How do you answer?","The stranger replies with a sketch of a doorway inside a library. What is written above it?","You receive two replies at once, each claiming to be the original. What evidence would distinguish them?","The final envelope contains a blank sheet. How do you choose to end the correspondence?"]},{"id":"constellation","title":"The Unfinished Constellation","kind":"learn","steps":["A fictional astronomer points out four stars and asks you to connect them with a story. What shape appears?","The telescope reveals an uncharted fifth point. Does it change the story or your idea of the map?","A second observer sees a different constellation from the same stars. What might both observations preserve?","You may submit a formal chart, a poem, or a question to the observatory archive. Which do you choose?"]},{"id":"kindness","title":"A Small Atlas of Kindness","kind":"notice","steps":["Choose one tiny act of care you have witnessed in ordinary life. Give it a map symbol.","Follow that symbol to a fictional neighborhood where everyone interprets it differently. What do they see?","Find a person who needs privacy more than help. What would respectful care look like?","Add a final landmark to your atlas, with no obligation to return to it."]},{"id":"impossible","title":"The Impossible Commission","kind":"play","steps":["A committee has hired you to solve an absurd municipal problem. What is the problem and its official name?","The committee rejects your sensible answer for an obviously ridiculous reason. How do you respond?","An unexpected witness proposes a simpler solution. Who are they?","The committee unveils your final invention at a disastrous ceremony. Describe the funniest harmless consequence."]}],"adventures":[{"id":"archive","title":"The Door in the Archive","category":"imagine","steps":[{"scene":"A library closes around you. Two doors remain: one labelled 'Questions' and one labelled 'Answers'.","options":["Questions","Answers"]},{"scene":"The librarian offers a map with one missing corner. You may ask who removed it or why it matters.","options":["Who removed it?","Why does it matter?"]},{"scene":"Beyond the shelf lies a courtyard with no roof. A single sign says 'This may be the beginning.'","options":["Write the beginning","Describe the courtyard"]}]},{"id":"clock","title":"The Clockmaker's Afternoon","category":"wander","steps":[{"scene":"A clockmaker presents a clock that loses only unimportant minutes.","options":["Ask for evidence","Try it safely"]},{"scene":"A second clock counts conversations instead of seconds.","options":["Compare the clocks","Ask who built it"]},{"scene":"The shop bell rings though nobody has entered.","options":["Investigate the bell","Invent an explanation"]}]},{"id":"observatory","title":"Night at the Observatory","category":"learn","steps":[{"scene":"An astronomer shows you a new star on an old chart.","options":["Check the chart","Check the telescope"]},{"scene":"Two instruments disagree, and both could be miscalibrated.","options":["Recheck the instruments","Ask what remains unknown"]},{"scene":"At sunrise the observatory requests a careful, uncertain report.","options":["Write the report","Ask one better question"]}]},{"id":"garden","title":"The Garden of Unfinished Things","category":"sacred","steps":[{"scene":"A garden gate opens only for visitors carrying an unfinished idea.","options":["Offer an idea","Ask about the rule"]},{"scene":"A gardener shows a repaired bench surrounded by seedlings.","options":["Ask about the repair","Describe what grows here"]},{"scene":"You may leave a label, a question, or nothing at all.","options":["Leave a question","Leave the space empty"]}]},{"id":"cartographer","title":"The Cartographer's Mistake","category":"reframe","steps":[{"scene":"A map leads everyone to the wrong bridge, but the bridge itself is real.","options":["Inspect the map","Interview a traveler"]},{"scene":"Two local guides disagree on the path but agree on the destination.","options":["Ask what each knows","Try a third route"]},{"scene":"You are asked to write the correction without humiliating its original author.","options":["Draft a correction","Draw a new legend"]}]},{"id":"theatre","title":"The Theatre of Tiny Disasters","category":"play","steps":[{"scene":"A stage manager announces that a spoon has stolen the entire production.","options":["Interview the spoon","Audit the props"]},{"scene":"A wardrobe of dramatic hats declares a strike.","options":["Negotiate fairly","Rewrite the scene"]},{"scene":"The audience arrives and expects a magnificent catastrophe.","options":["Improvise an ending","Let the props perform"]}]}],"collisions":[["a lighthouse","an unfinished apology","Both attempt to make something visible across a distance."],["a train timetable","a personal boundary","Both make expectations clearer only when others can read them."],["a library catalogue","a constellation","Both are systems for finding relationships among far-apart things."],["an old key","a creative block","A useful shape may outlive the door it was designed for."],["a repaired bicycle","a long friendship","Maintenance is evidence of continued choice, not failure."],["a seed bank","an oral-history archive","Both preserve possibilities beyond the lifetimes of individual keepers."],["a weather forecast","a difficult prediction","Uncertainty matters as much as the headline."],["a museum label","an online argument","What we leave out affects what others believe happened."],["a neighborhood garden","an unlikely alliance","Cooperation can emerge from different needs rather than identical beliefs."],["a musical rest","a conversation","Silence can be structure rather than absence."],["a river delta","a changed opinion","One origin can produce several valid routes forward."],["a telescope","a misunderstanding","Both are altered by where we stand and what instrument we use."],["a recipe","an inherited tradition","Rules can be useful without becoming sacred."],["a board game","a workplace rule","The rules reveal whose choices the system values."],["a broken clock","a memory","Both can feel precise while requiring outside checks."],["a train platform","a goodbye","A threshold can be an ordinary place and an extraordinary moment."],["a compass","a promise","Direction matters most when there is more than one possible path."],["a city map","a family story","Each highlights some places and leaves others off the page."],["a ghost story","an old law","Both reveal what a community is afraid to name."],["a bicycle bell","a public apology","A small signal can create space if someone listens."],["a field guide","a diary","Close observation need not become a judgment."],["a glacier","a long-term commitment","Change can be difficult to notice while still being continuous."],["a bridge","a translation","Both exist because separation should not make contact impossible."],["a kite","a choice","Freedom and constraint can be part of the same structure."],["an empty stage","a blank journal","An unused space can be an invitation rather than a lack."],["a lighthouse beam","a difficult truth","Visibility does not guarantee that anybody understands the signal."],["an astronomical atlas","a rumor","A map of points becomes meaningful only through how they are connected."],["a tree ring","a creative revision","Growth can leave visible evidence of interruption."],["a library return slip","a second chance","Both assume that something can come back changed."],["a public square","a private belief","Shared space tests the difference between disagreement and coercion."],["a traffic sign","a social convention","One is written down; the other can still control behavior."],["a childhood toy","a scientific model","A small representation can help us understand something larger without becoming that thing."],["a garden path","a creative detour","The route becomes part of what you discover."],["a radio broadcast","a lost letter","Both depend on an imagined recipient."],["a theatre costume","a first impression","Visible signals are not the whole person."],["a museum restoration","a sincere apology","Neither needs to pretend the damage never happened."]],"physical":[{"question":"Find an object near you with visible evidence of use. What might it have witnessed?","alternate":"Imagine a well-loved ordinary object. What marks would tell its story?"},{"question":"Listen for the quietest sound you can notice without moving. What does it add to the room?","alternate":"Imagine the soundscape of a familiar room and name its quietest sound."},{"question":"Look at the edges of a familiar object. What choices shaped them?","alternate":"Picture an ordinary cup. How does its shape reveal its purpose?"},{"question":"Find a place where two materials meet. What would a designer notice?","alternate":"Imagine a wooden table with a metal leg. What makes the join work?"},{"question":"Notice the quality of light from where you are sitting. Describe it without an emotion word.","alternate":"Imagine late-afternoon light falling into a quiet library. Describe only what is visible."},{"question":"Find something that was repaired or adapted. What small improvement did it gain?","alternate":"Imagine a repaired jacket. What story might its stitching tell?"},{"question":"Look for a sign, label, or small instruction near you. Who is its intended reader?","alternate":"Imagine a sign at an empty train platform. Who was it written for?"},{"question":"Choose an object you can describe using only texture and weight.","alternate":"Describe the imagined texture and weight of a smooth stone."},{"question":"Notice an everyday convenience you rarely think about. Which invisible work makes it possible?","alternate":"Imagine a drinking-water faucet. What invisible work makes it useful?"}],"lenses":[{"id":"archivist","name":"The Archivist","question":"Which exact detail would you preserve for someone who wasn't there?"},{"id":"witness","name":"The Witness","question":"What could you honestly say you observed, apart from what you inferred?"},{"id":"skeptic","name":"The Skeptic","question":"What explanation might be wrong, and what would fairly test it?"},{"id":"cartographer","name":"The Cartographer","question":"What connections does the apparent route leave out?"},{"id":"fool","name":"The Fool","question":"What is quietly absurd here, without making anybody the joke?"},{"id":"gardener","name":"The Gardener","question":"What might grow if you gave this less force and more time?"}],"transformations":{"gentler":"What is one small, optional part of this that feels approachable right now?","concrete":"Name one observable detail and one practical next step.","stranger":"Reimagine the premise in a city where one ordinary rule no longer applies.","fiction":"Give the question to a fictional character with something to lose.","challenging":"What assumption would a fair-minded skeptic ask you to test?","different":"Choose a completely different doorway instead of rephrasing this one."}};globalThis.ElsewhereInfiniteContent=Object.freeze(CONTENT);})();
